notes: Wave 2. Instruction-law crates that are directories with a crate folder but not workspace members currently sit beside runtime protocol crates and look like kernel modules. Double-check found 41 leftover HAS_CRATE directories rather than the five names in the first draft. They are admit-no-trust-tier, admit-opa-sole, admit-parity, admit-trust-floor, agent-sign-key-provision, caw-wrapenv-failclosed, client-trust-tier-ignore, connector-ucb-clients, dynaep-live-crossing-e2e, empty-lattice-close, envelope-algebra, envelope-algebra-ci, envelope-journals-drop, envelope-product-copy, envelope-wrap-disabled, envelope-wrap-journals, eu-ai-act-checker, frame-header-binding, gap-capability-dimensions, hyperlattice-ssot, kernel-pq-channel, lattice-db-parent-guard, lattice-log-record-admit, library-layer-count, live-crossing-admit-apply, live-crossing-lab-off, live-crossing-reject-copy, live-entry-ci, mesh-ca-secret-mode, named-surfaces, no-sequential-ts-deny, one-admit-id, one-evaluation-story, one-live-entry-language, potomitan-mesh-packet-plane, process-event-admit-walls, satisfied-actions-partition, sdk-run-meet-park, stream-hard-findings, trust-score-isolation and version-ssot. Live enforcement for those laws already runs inside aep-base-node source_invariants folded_slogan_ci_gates. Relocate the duplicate directories to retired-archive/instruction-crates so AEP-Components is not a second product. Write retired-archive/instruction-crates/INVENTORY.gaplune listing each relocated crate, its closed parent ticket and the gate that still runs it. Keep companion folders that have no crate and are not leftover scanners: aep-comm, aepassist, caw-framework, cca, coding-governance, covenant, datasets, decomposition, economics, eval, evidence-ledger, fleet, gap, graph-engine, hcse, hyperlattice, identity, intent, intent-ledger, intercept, knowledge-base, mcp-security, model-gateway, optimization, permissions, policy-engine, proof-bundle, proxy, recovery, scanners, semantic-topology, session, streaming, telemetry, verification, wizard and workflow. Trust Rings is owned by AEP28-ENV-075 and must already be absent. Do not add leftover crates to workspace members. Do not delete source_invariants folded gates. After the move, any remaining cargo test -p leftover-package scripts must use the new folder or source_invariants. A new HAS_CRATE directory under AEP-Components that is not a workspace member must fail source_invariants.
acceptance: None of the 41 leftover HAS_CRATE names remain under AEP-Components. None of them appear in workspace members. Companion folders listed in notes still exist under AEP-Components. Trust Rings is absent from AEP-Components. retired-archive/instruction-crates holds the relocated crates plus INVENTORY.gaplune. cargo test -p aep-base-node --test source_invariants still runs folded_slogan_ci_gates. source_invariants fails if a new non-member HAS_CRATE directory appears under AEP-Components. scripts/gate-aep28-env-073.sh covers the inventory and the non-member probe. nla-policy-scan gate coding-completion and project-completion-bac on AEP-Base-Node crate.
